<!-- TAB 16: SEO, Reporting & Tracking -->
<div id="sheet16">
<table>
<tr><th colspan="11" style="font-size:16pt; background-color:#0A0A0A; color:#FFFFFF;">SEO, Reporting &amp; Tracking — Elementor Build Guide</th></tr>

<!-- SECTION A: ESSENTIAL PLUGINS -->
<tr class="section-header"><td colspan="11" style="background-color:#0A0A0A; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:bold;">SECTION A: ESSENTIAL WORDPRESS PLUGINS</td></tr>

<tr style="background-color:#D95A2B; color:#FFFFFF;">
<th colspan="4">Plugin</th><th colspan="4">Purpose</th><th colspan="3">Free / Paid</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="4">Yoast SEO</td>
<td colspan="4">On-page SEO, XML sitemaps, meta tags, schema markup, breadcrumbs, content analysis</td>
<td colspan="3">Free (Pro optional — adds redirect manager, internal linking suggestions, multiple focus keywords)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="4">Google Site Kit</td>
<td colspan="4">Connects Google Analytics, Search Console, PageSpeed Insights, and AdSense directly in the WordPress dashboard</td>
<td colspan="3">Free</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="4">MonsterInsights</td>
<td colspan="4">GA4 integration with in-dashboard reports, real-time stats, eCommerce tracking, and custom dimensions</td>
<td colspan="3">Free (Pro optional — adds advanced tracking, eCommerce reports, form conversions)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="4">WP Rocket</td>
<td colspan="4">Page caching, browser caching, GZIP compression, CSS/JS minification, lazy loading images, database optimization</td>
<td colspan="3">Paid ($59/year single site)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="4">Smush</td>
<td colspan="4">Image compression and optimization, lazy loading, WebP conversion, bulk optimization</td>
<td colspan="3">Free (Pro optional — adds CDN, lossy compression, no size limits)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="4">Redirection</td>
<td colspan="4">301 redirect management, 404 error tracking, automatic URL monitoring, import/export redirects</td>
<td colspan="3">Free</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="4">UpdraftPlus</td>
<td colspan="4">Automated scheduled backups to cloud storage (Google Drive, Dropbox, S3), one-click restore</td>
<td colspan="3">Free (Premium optional — adds incremental backups, migration, multisite)</td>
</tr>

<!-- SECTION B: GA4 SETUP -->
<tr class="section-header"><td colspan="11" style="background-color:#0A0A0A; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:bold;">SECTION B: GA4 SETUP</td></tr>

<tr style="background-color:#D95A2B; color:#FFFFFF;">
<th colspan="2">Step</th><th colspan="4">Action</th><th colspan="5">Details</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">B.1</td>
<td colspan="4">Create GA4 Property</td>
<td colspan="5">Go to analytics.google.com > Admin > Create Property. Property name: "Mercy Court RCCG". Time zone: Eastern (US). Currency: USD.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">B.2</td>
<td colspan="4">Set Up Web Data Stream</td>
<td colspan="5">Add a Web stream with URL: https://mercycourt.org. Stream name: "Mercy Court Website". Enable Enhanced Measurement (page views, scrolls, outbound clicks, site search, video engagement, file downloads).</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">B.3</td>
<td colspan="4">Install Tracking Code</td>
<td colspan="5">Copy the Measurement ID (G-XXXXXXXXXX). Install via Google Site Kit plugin (recommended) or manually paste the gtag.js snippet into the site header using Elementor Custom Code or a header/footer plugin.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">B.4</td>
<td colspan="4">Configure Events</td>
<td colspan="5">Set up custom events for: give_button_click, contact_form_submit, mailing_list_signup, watch_live_visit, phone_click, social_link_click. Use GA4 Event Builder or Google Tag Manager.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">B.5</td>
<td colspan="4">Set Up Conversions</td>
<td colspan="5">Mark key events as conversions: give_button_click, contact_form_submit, mailing_list_signup. Go to Admin > Events > toggle "Mark as conversion".</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">B.6</td>
<td colspan="4">Link Google Search Console</td>
<td colspan="5">In GA4 Admin > Product Links > Search Console Links > Link. This enables search query data in GA4 reports.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">B.7</td>
<td colspan="4">Set Up Audiences</td>
<td colspan="5">Create audiences: "Give Page Visitors" (visited /give), "Blog Readers" (visited /blog/*), "New Visitors" (session count = 1), "Returning Visitors" (session count > 1), "Watch Live Visitors" (visited /watch-live).</td>
</tr>

<!-- SECTION C: GOOGLE SEARCH CONSOLE -->
<tr class="section-header"><td colspan="11" style="background-color:#0A0A0A; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:bold;">SECTION C: GOOGLE SEARCH CONSOLE SETUP</td></tr>

<tr style="background-color:#D95A2B; color:#FFFFFF;">
<th colspan="2">Step</th><th colspan="4">Action</th><th colspan="5">Details</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">C.1</td>
<td colspan="4">Verify Site Ownership</td>
<td colspan="5">Go to search.google.com/search-console. Add property: https://mercycourt.org. Verify via DNS TXT record (recommended) or HTML file upload or Google Site Kit plugin.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">C.2</td>
<td colspan="4">Submit XML Sitemap</td>
<td colspan="5">Go to Sitemaps > Add new sitemap. URL: https://mercycourt.org/sitemap_index.xml (generated by Yoast SEO). Verify it is accepted with no errors.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">C.3</td>
<td colspan="4">Request Indexing</td>
<td colspan="5">Use URL Inspection tool to submit all key pages for indexing: homepage, about, ministries, give, contact, blog, watch-live, quick-links, mercy-kidz, the-new-mc. Monitor coverage report for errors.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">C.4</td>
<td colspan="4">Monitor Performance</td>
<td colspan="5">Review Search Performance report weekly: total clicks, impressions, CTR, average position. Filter by query, page, country, device. Look for keyword opportunities with high impressions but low CTR.</td>
</tr>

<!-- SECTION D: ON-PAGE SEO CHECKLIST -->
<tr class="section-header"><td colspan="11" style="background-color:#0A0A0A; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:bold;">SECTION D: ON-PAGE SEO CHECKLIST (Per Page)</td></tr>

<tr style="background-color:#D95A2B; color:#FFFFFF;">
<th colspan="2">Element</th><th colspan="3">Requirement</th><th colspan="3">Example (Homepage)</th><th colspan="3">Notes</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">Page Title (Title Tag)</td>
<td colspan="3">50-60 characters, include primary keyword, brand name at end</td>
<td colspan="3">Mercy Court RCCG | Church in Baltimore, MD</td>
<td colspan="3">Set via Yoast SEO "SEO Title" field. Use pipe separator. Each page must have unique title.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">Meta Description</td>
<td colspan="3">150-160 characters, include call-to-action, mention location</td>
<td colspan="3">Join Mercy Court RCCG in Baltimore — experience God, enjoy life, and find your community. Sunday services at 10 AM. Visit us at 529 Walker Avenue.</td>
<td colspan="3">Set via Yoast SEO "Meta description" field. Must be unique per page. Include relevant keywords naturally.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">H1 Tag</td>
<td colspan="3">One per page, include primary keyword, match page purpose</td>
<td colspan="3">Welcome to Mercy Court RCCG — The Home of Pacesetters</td>
<td colspan="3">Only one H1 per page. Should be the most prominent heading on the page.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">Image Alt Text</td>
<td colspan="3">Descriptive, include keywords where natural, under 125 characters</td>
<td colspan="3">"Mercy Court RCCG congregation worshipping during Sunday service in Baltimore"</td>
<td colspan="3">Every image must have alt text. Avoid keyword stuffing. Describe the image accurately.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">URL Structure</td>
<td colspan="3">Short, descriptive, lowercase, hyphens for spaces, no special characters</td>
<td colspan="3">mercycourt.org/who-we-are, mercycourt.org/give, mercycourt.org/mercy-kidz</td>
<td colspan="3">Set WordPress permalinks to "Post name" structure. Avoid date-based or numeric URLs.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">Internal Links</td>
<td colspan="3">Link to related pages from content, use descriptive anchor text</td>
<td colspan="3">From Homepage: link to About, Ministries, Give, Blog. From Blog posts: link to related posts and key pages.</td>
<td colspan="3">Aim for 3-5 internal links per page. Helps search engines discover content and distributes page authority.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="2">Schema Markup</td>
<td colspan="3">Add structured data for Church, LocalBusiness, Events, Articles</td>
<td colspan="3">Organization schema with name, address (529 Walker Avenue, Baltimore, MD 21212), phone (+1 410-900-9111), logo, social profiles</td>
<td colspan="3">Use Yoast SEO schema settings or add custom JSON-LD in header. Test with Google Rich Results Test tool.</td>
</tr>

<!-- SECTION E: TECHNICAL SEO -->
<tr class="section-header"><td colspan="11" style="background-color:#0A0A0A; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:bold;">SECTION E: TECHNICAL SEO</td></tr>

<tr style="background-color:#D95A2B; color:#FFFFFF;">
<th colspan="3">Item</th><th colspan="4">Requirement</th><th colspan="4">Implementation</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">SSL Certificate</td>
<td colspan="4">Site must load via HTTPS. All pages, images, and assets must use HTTPS.</td>
<td colspan="4">Ensure hosting provider has SSL enabled. Force HTTPS redirect in .htaccess or via hosting panel. Check for mixed content warnings.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Mobile Responsiveness</td>
<td colspan="4">All pages must pass Google Mobile-Friendly Test. Touch targets min 48px.</td>
<td colspan="4">Test every page with Chrome DevTools responsive mode. Use Google Mobile-Friendly Test. Fix any viewport or tap target issues.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Page Speed</td>
<td colspan="4">Target: 90+ on PageSpeed Insights (both mobile and desktop)</td>
<td colspan="4">Use WP Rocket for caching + minification. Smush for images. Lazy load below-fold images. Minimize render-blocking CSS/JS. Use CDN if available.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">XML Sitemap</td>
<td colspan="4">Auto-generated sitemap including all public pages and posts</td>
<td colspan="4">Yoast SEO generates this automatically at /sitemap_index.xml. Submit to Google Search Console. Exclude noindex pages.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Robots.txt</td>
<td colspan="4">Allow search engine crawling, block admin and sensitive directories</td>
<td colspan="4">Default WordPress robots.txt is usually sufficient. Add: Disallow: /wp-admin/. Allow: /wp-admin/admin-ajax.php. Sitemap: https://mercycourt.org/sitemap_index.xml</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Canonical URLs</td>
<td colspan="4">Every page must have a canonical URL to prevent duplicate content</td>
<td colspan="4">Yoast SEO adds canonical tags automatically. Verify in page source: link rel="canonical". Ensure www vs non-www is consistent.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">301 Redirects</td>
<td colspan="4">Redirect old/changed URLs to new destinations. No 404 errors for important pages.</td>
<td colspan="4">Use Redirection plugin. Monitor 404 log regularly. Set up redirects for any URL changes during migration/redesign.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Structured Data</td>
<td colspan="4">Add JSON-LD structured data for Church, Events, Articles, FAQs</td>
<td colspan="4">Use Yoast SEO schema + custom JSON-LD blocks. Test with Google Rich Results Test. Add FAQ schema to Mercy Kidz FAQ section.</td>
</tr>

<!-- SECTION F: LOCAL SEO -->
<tr class="section-header"><td colspan="11" style="background-color:#0A0A0A; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:bold;">SECTION F: LOCAL SEO</td></tr>

<tr style="background-color:#D95A2B; color:#FFFFFF;">
<th colspan="3">Item</th><th colspan="4">Details</th><th colspan="4">Notes</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Google Business Profile</td>
<td colspan="4">Business Name: Mercy Court RCCG. Address: 529 Walker Avenue, Baltimore, MD 21212. Phone: +1 (410) 900-9111. Website: https://mercycourt.org. Category: Church, Religious Organization.</td>
<td colspan="4">Claim and verify the profile at business.google.com. Keep all info consistent with website. Add high-quality photos of the church, services, and events.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">NAP Consistency</td>
<td colspan="4">Name, Address, Phone must be identical everywhere: website footer, Google Business Profile, social media, directories</td>
<td colspan="4">Format: Mercy Court RCCG | 529 Walker Avenue, Baltimore, MD 21212 | +1 (410) 900-9111. Check Yelp, Facebook, Apple Maps for consistency.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Business Categories</td>
<td colspan="4">Primary: Church. Secondary: Religious Organization, Non-Denominational Church, Youth Organization</td>
<td colspan="4">Set in Google Business Profile. Choose the most specific primary category available.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Business Hours</td>
<td colspan="4">Sunday: 10:00 AM - 1:00 PM (Main Service). Add special hours for midweek services and events.</td>
<td colspan="4">Keep updated in Google Business Profile. Add holiday hours when applicable.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Photos</td>
<td colspan="4">Upload 10+ high-quality photos: exterior, interior, services, events, leadership, community outreach</td>
<td colspan="4">Add new photos monthly. Use geo-tagged images when possible. Include logo as profile photo.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Reviews</td>
<td colspan="4">Encourage congregation to leave Google reviews. Respond to all reviews within 48 hours.</td>
<td colspan="4">Add a "Leave a Review" link on the website. Include in email newsletters. Respond professionally to both positive and negative reviews.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Google Posts</td>
<td colspan="4">Publish weekly updates: upcoming events, service highlights, blog post links, announcements</td>
<td colspan="4">Posts expire after 7 days. Include CTA button (Learn More, Sign Up, Call Now). Add relevant image with each post.</td>
</tr>

<!-- SECTION G: SOCIAL MEDIA TRACKING -->
<tr class="section-header"><td colspan="11" style="background-color:#0A0A0A; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:bold;">SECTION G: SOCIAL MEDIA TRACKING</td></tr>

<tr style="background-color:#D95A2B; color:#FFFFFF;">
<th colspan="3">Item</th><th colspan="4">Implementation</th><th colspan="4">Notes</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Facebook Pixel</td>
<td colspan="4">Install Meta Pixel on all pages. Track PageView, ViewContent, Lead (form submissions), and InitiateCheckout (give page) events.</td>
<td colspan="4">Install via header code or PixelYourSite plugin. Create Custom Audiences for retargeting: website visitors, give page visitors, blog readers.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">UTM Parameters</td>
<td colspan="4">Use UTM tags on all social media links. Format: utm_source=facebook&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_campaign=sunday_service</td>
<td colspan="4">Create UTM links using Google Campaign URL Builder. Track in GA4 under Acquisition > Traffic Acquisition. Standardize naming conventions.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Social Meta Tags (Open Graph)</td>
<td colspan="4">Set og:title, og:description, og:image, og:url for every page. Twitter card tags: twitter:card=summary_large_image</td>
<td colspan="4">Yoast SEO handles this automatically via Social tab. Set default sharing image (1200x630px) with Mercy Court branding. Test with Facebook Sharing Debugger.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Social Profiles in Schema</td>
<td colspan="4">Add social profile URLs to Organization schema: Facebook, Instagram, YouTube</td>
<td colspan="4">Configure in Yoast SEO > Social. URLs: facebook.com/mercycourtrccg, instagram.com/mercycourtrccg, youtube.com/mercycourtrccg</td>
</tr>

<!-- SECTION H: EVENT & GOAL TRACKING -->
