<td colspan="3">Site Speed</td>
<td colspan="3">PageSpeed Insights / Google Site Kit</td>
<td colspan="2">Monthly</td>
<td colspan="3">Core Web Vitals: LCP (target &lt;2.5s), FID (target &lt;100ms), CLS (target &lt;0.1). Mobile and desktop scores (target 90+).</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Uptime Monitoring</td>
<td colspan="3">UptimeRobot (free) or hosting provider</td>
<td colspan="2">Continuous</td>
<td colspan="3">99.9% uptime target. Alerts for downtime via email/SMS. Monitor response time.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Backups</td>
<td colspan="3">UpdraftPlus</td>
<td colspan="2">Daily (automated)</td>
<td colspan="3">Full site backup (files + database). Store on Google Drive or Dropbox. Test restore monthly. Keep 30-day retention.</td>
</tr>

<!-- SECTION J: CONTENT & BLOG SEO STRATEGY -->
<tr class="section-header"><td colspan="11" style="background-color:#0A0A0A; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:bold;">SECTION J: CONTENT &amp; BLOG SEO STRATEGY</td></tr>

<tr style="background-color:#D95A2B; color:#FFFFFF;">
<th colspan="3">Item</th><th colspan="4">Details</th><th colspan="4">Notes</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Posting Frequency</td>
<td colspan="4">2-4 blog posts per month. Consistent schedule (e.g., every Monday and Thursday).</td>
<td colspan="4">Quality over quantity. Each post should be 500-1500 words. Include images and internal links.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Keyword Research</td>
<td colspan="4">Use Google Keyword Planner, Ubersuggest, or AnswerThePublic. Focus on local + intent keywords.</td>
<td colspan="4">Primary research quarterly. Track keyword rankings monthly. Look for low-competition, high-intent terms.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Target Keywords</td>
<td colspan="4">Primary: "church in Baltimore", "RCCG Baltimore", "Mercy Court RCCG". Secondary: "Baltimore church near me", "non-denominational church Baltimore", "youth church Baltimore", "kids church Baltimore MD", "give to church online", "church live stream Baltimore"</td>
<td colspan="4">Use naturally in page titles, headings, meta descriptions, and body content. Don't keyword stuff. Include in image alt text where relevant.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Content Categories</td>
<td colspan="4">News, Events, Devotionals, Testimonies, Announcements (match blog filter categories)</td>
<td colspan="4">Create WordPress categories matching these. Use categories in Yoast SEO breadcrumbs. Each post should have exactly one primary category.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Internal Linking Strategy</td>
<td colspan="4">Every blog post should link to: 1 key page (Give, About, Ministries), 1-2 related blog posts, relevant Quick Links</td>
<td colspan="4">Use descriptive anchor text (not "click here"). Yoast SEO Pro offers internal linking suggestions. Review and update old posts with links to new content.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Featured Images</td>
<td colspan="4">Every post needs a featured image. Size: 1200x630px (optimal for social sharing). Compress to under 200KB.</td>
<td colspan="4">Use consistent branding (Mercy Court colors, logo watermark). Add alt text. Use Smush to auto-compress on upload.</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td colspan="3">Meta Descriptions for Posts</td>
<td colspan="4">Unique 150-160 char description for every post. Include call-to-action and relevant keyword.</td>
<td colspan="4">Set via Yoast SEO on each post. If not set manually, Yoast auto-generates from first paragraph — always customize.</td>
</tr>

</table>
</div>
</body></html>
